{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalDiracOperatorUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalDiracOperatorUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QDifferentialGeometry","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalDirac.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalDirac.unique","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-unique.lean#L27-L59","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical Dirac operator.**\n\nGiven fixed connection, substrate parameter `q` / inverse `qinv`, and\nReeb data `nablaEndo` (`∇`) and `reeb` (`ι_ξ∇`), the operator\n`𝒟_∇ = q⁻¹ ∇ + (1 - q⁻¹) ι_ξ∇` is uniquely determined: the `dirac`\nmorphism is forced by [`def:categorical-dirac-operator`]'s\n`dirac_formula`, so two such operators are equal.\n\nThis replaces the earlier `axiom … : Subsingleton (CategoricalDiracOperator …)`,\nwhich was **false** (the structure has free fields, so distinct data give\ndistinct operators).  Uniqueness holds only conditionally on shared data —\nexactly the narrative claim. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-dirac-operator-unique","label":"prop:categorical-dirac-operator-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}